1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Previously on Elephant Dar is I met up with an old friend Wendy.
之前在大象达尔，我遇到了一位老朋友温迪。

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
She seems to be having a bit of an identity crisis.
她似乎正面临某种身份认同的危机。

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
More interested in interacting with people than elephants.
比起与大象相处，她更喜欢与人交往。

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
And a tiny three-week-old baby elephant was rescued when he collapsed in the wild.
还有一只仅三周大的小象在野外倒下时被救了。

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:26,000
After a few days in the orphanage in Nairobi, Deathly made a devastating discovery.
在内罗毕的孤儿院里待了几天后，Deathly有了惊人的发现。

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
And for she, one eyes blondens, the other one looks like it's came bright.
她的眼睛，一只是金色的，另一只则看起来很明亮。

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Say we've got a bland elephant.
我们有一只口味不好的大象。

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
We're following the stories of a group of orphaned baby elephants in Kenya.
我们正在追踪一群在肯尼亚的孤儿小象的故事。

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
All of them have been rescued by the David Shundrick Wildlife Trust
它们都被大卫·舒德里克野生动物基金会救了出来，

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
and brought to a unique orphanage in Nairobi.
并被送到了内罗毕的一家独特的孤儿院。

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Here they're reared and nurtured by a teen of 20 dedicated kiddos
它们由20岁的志愿者抚养长大。

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
under the guidance of the orphanage founder, Dane Daffney-Shundrick.
在孤儿院创始人戴恩·达夫尼-舒德里克的指导下。

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
The ultimate aim is to get them back to the wild in Sarbo National Park.
最终目标是将它们送回萨博国家公园的野外生活。

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Undololo is the newest arrival and despite his blindness he's making steady progress.
乌多洛是最新加入的孤儿，尽管他失明，但仍在稳步进步。

15
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,000
The other orphans are out in the bush, but for now Undololo is being kept in isolation.
其他孤儿都在野外生活，不过目前乌多洛被隔离了起来。

16
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Everyone adores him, especially head keeper Edwin.
大家都很崇拜他，尤其是主管埃德温。

17
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
It's a very clever boy, very selective.
他是个非常聪明的孩子，很会选择。

18
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:56,000
But because at the moment he tries to smell around all the hippas and can find out the favorites among the hippas.
但是因为此刻他试图在所有的河马周围嗅探，从而能找出其中最受欢迎的那只河马。

19
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,000
And in return they attend to his every mood, protecting his delicate ears with sun cream
作为回报，她们会关注他的每一丝情绪，用防晒霜保护他敏感的耳朵，让他免受正午阳光的照射。

20
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
and shading him from the midday sun.
并遮挡他免受烈日炙烤。

21
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
They determined to give him the best chance of survival
他们决心给他最好的生存机会。

22
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
and what's giving everyone hope is that the vet thinks his blindness might be curable.
让所有人充满希望的是，兽医认为他的失明可能是可以治愈的。

23
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:19,000
As everybody is pity about him and everybody is worried about him.
因为大家都很同情他，也都为他担心。

24
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:24,000
So everybody wants to take care of him. Everybody wants to be concerned with him.
所以大家都想照顾他，希望能关心他。

25
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,000
And we want to be close to him to see that he cannot help him improve.
我们希望能靠近他，看看他能否有所改善。

26
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Only time will tell if his eyesight will get better.
只有时间能证明他的视力是否会好转。

27
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
But hopefully he should be well enough to meet the other little orphans very soon.
但希望他能尽快康复，能够与其他小孤儿们见面。

28
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
But for now playing with the big boys and girls is out of the question.
不过目前，和他一起和大的男孩、女孩玩耍是不可能的。

29
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Their games are far too exciting and there's a reason for this.
他们的游戏太刺激了，这是有原因的。

30
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
All of these elephants have had a really tough start to life.
这些大象的起步都很艰难。

31
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:55,000
They've all experienced tragedy and they've all had to grow up and learn lessons far quicker than they would have done in the wild.
他们都经历了悲剧，而且他们都必须比在野外时更快地成长并吸取教训。

32
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:02,000
But nevertheless they're still very young so it's still important for them to get some exercise, let off some steam and have some fun.
不过他们仍然很年轻，因此让他们进行一些锻炼、释放能量、享受乐趣还是非常重要的。

33
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:11,000
And what better way to do that than a good old game of football?
还有什么比踢一场好的足球比赛更好的方式呢？

34
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:16,000
These games are more than just a chance for the orphans to run rings around the keepers.
这些比赛不仅仅是孤儿们战胜守门员的机会。

35
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Train is a great way for this little herd of unrelated babies to bond with each other.
训练是让这群不相关的婴儿相互建立联系的好方法。

36
00:03:46,000 --> 00:04:07,000
[Music]
[音乐]

37
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,000
The friendships the little elephants form here in my baby are for life.
这些小象在这里建立的友谊将伴随他们一生。

38
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Because when you've lost your family, friends are all you've got.
因为当你失去家庭后，朋友就是你唯一的依靠了。

39
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:20,000
And these bonds will stay with the orphans as they reach the age to leave the nursery
这些关系会在孤儿们长大到可以离开托儿所时继续存在。

40
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:25,000
and go through to the next stage in their journey back to the wild.
然后他们就能进入回归野外的下一阶段。

41
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:31,000
And this second stage is the one I'm following down here in Savo National Park.
第二阶段就是我现在正在萨沃国家公园里进行的这段旅程。

42
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:37,000
I'm on my way to one of the trust two release sites to catch up with an orphan called Wendy.
我正前往两个被管理的放养地点之一，去接一个名叫温迪的孤儿。

43
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,000
This is a film brand, it has to be one of the wildest places in Kenya.
这里是一个电影拍摄地，肯定是肯尼亚最荒野的地方之一。

44
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:48,000
But it's also where the little elephants from Myrobi orphanage are brought to begin the process of introducing them back into the wild.
但这也是米罗比孤儿院的小象们被带到这里开始回归野外生活的过程的地点。

45
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:56,000
But not only is it wild, it is stunningly beautiful and a safe haven for the elephants too. Perfect.
这里不仅荒野十足，而且风景绝美，也是大象的安全栖息地。真是完美。

46
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Down here the elephants spend the night in open-air stockades and go out into the bush each day to learn everything they need to know about life in the wild.
在这里，大象们会在露天围栏里过夜，每天都会进入灌木丛里，以学习关于野外生活所需的一切知识。

47
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:13,000
But my main concern here at the moment is to see how Wendy is getting on.
但目前我最关心的是温迪的情况如何。

48
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:18,000
At the age of four, she should be settled into life with her elephant family
四岁时，她应该已经与大象家族一起适应生活了。

49
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,000
and forming close bonds with other females in her head.
并且与其他雌性大象建立了亲密的关系。

50
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:28,000
But because she was raised by humans from the day she was born, Wendy has other ideas.
但由于她从出生起就由人类抚养长大，温迪有着不同的想法。

51
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:34,000
You can see how Wendy, really at the moment, is much more interested in people than she is in the other elephants.
现在可以看出，温迪对人类的兴趣远远高于对其他大象的兴趣。

52
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:39,000
I mean she's completely isolated here, that's not what we want. We want her to be an elephant.
我的意思是，她现在完全被孤立了，这不是我们想要的。我们希望她能继续做一头大象。

53
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:47,000
But at the same time we are her family, the keepers of her family, we have to play that role for her if it's what she needs.
但与此同时，我们也是她的家人，是她的守护者，如果她需要的话，我们就必须扮演这个角色。

54
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
And each of these animals are very distinct characters.
这些动物每一个都有着独特的性格。

55
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Right now Wendy seems almost lonely at times as if she doesn't quite know what to do with herself.
目前，温迪有时看起来很孤独，似乎不知道该如何应对。

56
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:04,000
This is a complex problem and shows how sensitive and intelligent elephants are.
这是一个复杂的问题，也显示出大象的敏感与智慧。

57
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:09,000
But Daphne and the keepers are hoping that they have come up with a solution.
但达芙妮和饲养员们希望他们能找到解决方案。

58
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Crucially it's something which will help her bond with other elephants.
重要的是，这个方案能帮助她与其他大象建立联系。

59
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:18,000
And it involves some of the little orphans up in Myrophy with Michaela.
它涉及到那些在米罗菲的孤儿们，包括米凯拉。

60
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:24,000
There are ten of them living here at the moment, but things are about to change.
目前这里有十只动物，但情况即将发生变化。

61
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:29,000
The nursery is a great place for all these orphans to start their journey back into the wild.
这个孤儿院是这些孤儿重新回归自然生活的好地方。

62
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:35,000
However they all get to an age around the age of two where they need to move on to the next stage of their rehabilitation.
不过，它们都到了两岁左右，需要进入下一个康复阶段。

63
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Now currently in this group there are three elephants that are big enough to make that move.
目前，这个群体中有三只大象足够大，可以完成这一转变。

64
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:49,000
So how is this going to help Wendy? When she was in Myrophy she was the mini matriarch and this is the key to the whole plan.
那么，这会对温迪有什么帮助呢？在米罗菲时，她就是小族长，这是整个计划的关键。

65
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:56,000
What they're going to do is when they move the new group of little elephants from the orphanage in Myrophy up here through Thumba,
他们的计划是，将新的一群小象从米罗菲的孤儿院带到这里，经过图姆巴后，

66
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:01,000
they're going to separate them in one part of the stockade and they're going to put Wendy with them.
他们会在围栏的某一部分将它们分开，然后把温迪也放在一起。

67
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Now that'll suddenly give her a roll again. It'll give her a purpose in life.
这样，她就能再次扮演起族长的角色，拥有生活的目标。

68
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:10,000
It'll make her a mini matriarch again. I just hope the plan works.
她会再次成为小族长。我只希望这个计划能成功。

69
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Here in Myrophy preparations are in full swing for this move which is due to happen early tomorrow morning.
在米罗菲，为这次转移所做的准备工作正在进行中，预计明天清晨就会进行。

70
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:27,000
So for the keepers it's time to say goodbye to the three who are leaving.
所以，管理员们是时候与那三只即将离开的象说再见了。

71
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Among them is a little elephant called a rock. He's the smallest and the most nervous of the three.
其中有一只名叫“Rock”的小象。它是三只中最小、最紧张的那只。

72
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:41,000
The move could be pretty stressful for him but he's really going to need a big friend like Wendy to take care of him.
这个行动对它来说可能相当有压力，但它真的需要像温迪那样强大的朋友来照顾它。

73
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:46,000
So it's as important for a rock as it is for Wendy that the plan works.
因此，计划能够成功，对“Rock”来说和对温迪一样重要。

74
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Back at the stables the trucks are ready and waiting to take all three to their new life.
回到马厩后，那些卡车已经准备就绪，准备把三只小动物带到新的生活环境中。

75
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:13,000
After an early start the three little lilies from Myrophy are well on their way down to join Wendy and the others here in Atumba.
经过早起的旅程后，来自米罗菲的三只小百合花正朝着与温迪及其他动物一起在阿通巴的方向前进。

76
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:22,000
It's eight pothamas in a truck driving deep into Savo National Park which will be home for the rest of their lives.
有八辆卡车将它们送往萨沃国家公园，那里将是它们余生居住的地方。

77
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:38,000
They seem none the worse for their ordeal although I have to say little a rock does look quite anxious.
它们似乎并没有因为这次经历而受到太大影响，不过不得不说，“Rock”看起来确实很焦虑。

78
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:45,000
They must be tough for them. Different voices, different sounds, different smells, a whole different place for them.
对它们来说，这一定很艰难。不同的声音、不同的气味、完全不同的环境……

79
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:52,000
But the one thing they've got of course is the keepers. The keepers are the continuity in this whole project.
但它们所拥有的唯一东西，就是那些照顾者。这些照顾者就是这个项目的延续性所在。

80
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:57,000
And wherever they are, in Myrophy, atumba they will be very much loved.
无论它们身处米罗菲还是阿通巴，它们都会受到深深的喜爱。

81
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:03,000
This one, the little this one, a rock you can tell.
这颗小石头，你能够看清楚它。

82
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:07,000
It's whole body language says I'm nervous, I'm not sure where I am.
它的全身姿态都表明我很紧张，不知道自己身处何方。

83
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:11,000
In eight hours you've moved me, you've changed my whole world.
八小时之内，你就改变了我，彻底改变了我的世界。

84
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Poor little a rock, I mean he looks so scared.
可怜的小石头，它看起来如此害怕。

85
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:22,000
He really does need a bigger elephant to take him under her wing and we're all hoping it's going to be Wendy.
它真的需要一只更大的大象来保护它，希望那大象是温迪吧。

86
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Okay, here come the other elephants and amongst them is Wendy, this could be crucial.
好吧，其他大象来了，其中就有温迪，这可能会很重要。

87
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Oh, no!
哦，不！

88
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Okay, what is that saying there?
好吧，那上面到底写着什么？

89
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:46,000
I reckon it says there's something going on here and I don't know how you want to know what it is.
我觉得上面写着这里发生了什么事情，不过我不知道你希望如何知道那是什么。

90
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:55,000
The whole herd is so excited and the little ones are being thoroughly checked over.
整个群体都非常兴奋，那些小动物也被仔细检查了。

91
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:01,000
It's reassuring, just touching and feeling. Are you okay? Everything's fine, don't worry.
只是触摸和感受一下，就让人安心了。你没事吧？一切都会好起来的，不用担心。

92
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
You're in a new place but it's going to be okay.
你身处一个新的地方，但一切都会好起来的。

93
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:08,000
A rock needs some reassurance, so where is Wendy?
石头也需要一些安慰，那么温迪在哪儿呢？

94
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:14,000
There she is and how typical she's taking no interest, just doing her own thing.
她就在那儿，她完全不感兴趣，只是做自己的事。

95
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:21,000
Let's hope the enthusiasm of the others rubs off on her and she starts to feel maternal towards these little ones.
希望其他人的热情能感染她，让她开始对这些小家伙产生母性关怀。

96
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:28,000
She's going to be put in charge of them in a stock A tonight and during the night is when a rock will need her most.
今晚她将负责照顾它们，而夜晚正是石头最需要她的时候。

97
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:35,000
But it's not only the Fumba herd meeting new friends.
不过，弗姆巴的群兽并非只有这一群新朋友。

98
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:42,000
Up in Nairobi, the keepers have decided that Underlolo is finally ready to meet the other orphans.
在内罗毕，饲养者们认为昂特洛洛终于可以与其他孤儿见面了。

99
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:47,000
He's been kept apart from them until now as he's been too hit to meet them.
直到现在，他一直被分开来，因为他太虚弱了，无法与它们见面。

100
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:53,000
And now he's getting so much stronger, it's time to say hello.
现在他变得强壮多了，是时候打招呼了。

101
00:10:53,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Despite their overwhelming curiosity, the bigger orphans are being very gentle and careful
尽管那些体型较大的孤儿充满好奇，但它们却非常温柔细心。

102
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:07,000
and seem to be able to sense Underlolo's fragility.
似乎能够感知到Underlolo的脆弱性。

103
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:15,000
But doting Edwin and the keepers are watching very closely to make sure their precious little elephant is coping.
但溺爱它的埃德温和饲养员们则密切注视着，确保他们珍贵的小象能够安然度过难关。

104
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:32,000
The meeting has gone well, but it will be a long time before Underlolo is ready to join the whole gang
会议进行得很顺利，但Underlolo还需要很长时间才能准备好与整个群体一起外出散步。

105
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,000
for their daily walks out into the bush.
去到灌木丛里散步。

106
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:41,000
And the little elephant is led back to his stables for a much needed rest.
小象被带回马厩里，以便得到必要的休息。

107
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Down here in Fumba, the alleys are heading for bed.
在芬巴这里，街道上的人都在准备睡觉。

108
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:57,000
An area of the stock A has been sectioned off so that Wendy can be put in charge of the three new arrivals.
库存A中的一部分区域被划分出来，让温迪负责照顾那三个新来的动物。

109
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:04,000
This is her chance to be a mini matriarch again and for a rock a chance to get some much needed TLC.
这是她再次成为小型族长的机会，也有机会得到应有的照顾。

110
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:08,000
So they look at kids with their first night at boarding school.
因此，他们看着那些在寄宿学校度过第一晚的孩子们。

111
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:13,000
The three new ones off by themselves, where they feel safe is with the keepers.
那三个新来的人，在守护者身边时才会感到安全。

112
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:17,000
The three that know the ropes, including Wendy, but just very relaxed, as you'd expect.
那三个熟悉情况的人，包括温迪，也显得很放松，正如你所预期的那样。

113
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,000
They know the routine here, and new ones don't yet.
他们已经熟悉了这里的规矩，而新来的人还不太熟悉。

114
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Little O'Rox means quite stressed and is looking for conflict, but now mine is interested.
小奥罗克斯看起来很紧张，一直在寻找冲突，不过现在我的猫却很感兴趣。

115
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:33,000
You can imagine how different low this is.
你可以想象，这里的压力有多大。

116
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:38,000
They set up for our three little elephants from Nairobi because normally, at this time of the day in the evening,
他们为我们在内罗毕的三只小象准备食物，因为通常在这个傍晚时分，它们会回到马厩里，与饲养员一起休息。

117
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,000
they'd be going back to a stable, their own place to sleep, with their keeper.
他们会回到一个稳定的环境里，回到自己睡觉的地方，与他们的饲养员一起。

118
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Suddenly, this is big and scary. What's this about?
突然间，这变得很可怕了。这到底是怎么回事呢？

119
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Poor Little O'Rox is getting pushed around, and it's windy that's doing it.
可怜的小奥罗克斯被推来推去，而风也助长了这种混乱状况。

120
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:58,000
There are a couple of other older elephants in there as well, and they're falling asleep, pushing and shoving.
还有几只年纪较大的大象也在那里，它们正在睡觉，却还在互相推挤。

121
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:01,000
This is not quite going to plan.
这并不完全符合计划。

122
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:05,000
But what they don't realise is they're being watched from next door.
但他们没有意识到，其实有人在隔壁看着他们。

123
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:09,000
You see the way Nussa loves. She's one of the bigger elephants.
你看，努萨多么爱孩子啊。她可是体型较大的大象之一。

124
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:13,000
It's just thinking, "What's happening here?"
只是想着：“这里到底发生了什么？”

125
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:17,000
I want to go and check those little ones out.
我想去看看那些小家伙们。

126
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,000
And that's exactly what you'd expect for one of these bigger elephants.
这正是大型大象通常会做的事。

127
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Acting as an auntie. She's not the matriarch, but she's a very, very caring elephant.
她扮演着阿姨的角色。虽然她不是族长，但她是位非常体贴的大象。

128
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:31,000
She's desperate to get in there and look after the little ones.
她非常想进去照顾那些小家伙们。

129
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
But this is supposed to be Wendy's job.
不过，这本应该是温迪的工作。

130
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:37,000
You know, Wendy is so naughty. It's not what I expected.
你知道，温迪太调皮了。这和我预想的不一样。

131
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:42,000
I was hoping that she was going to sort of smother these little ones with a bit of love.
我希望她能用爱来抚平这些小家伙的不安。

132
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
But it's just like, you know, "What are you doing here?"
但就是，你知道的， “你在这里做什么？”

133
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
And she's pushing them out of the way. You can see it like that.
她把它们推开到一边。你可以看到那样子。

134
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Actually getting quite shovey, quite bushy.
实际上，它们变得很茂盛、很浓密了。

135
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Hang on, what's this?
等等，这是什么？

136
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Okay, the keepers are putting Nussa lot in with the little ones.
好吧，那些饲养员正在把努萨和那些小家伙放在一起。

137
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
And they certainly look pleased to see her.
它们看起来显然很开心能见到她。

138
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Just a look at them.
看看它们吧。

139
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:11,000
Now that's interesting. That was Wendy just being basically told, sorry.
真有趣。温迪基本上就是被告知了“对不起”而已。

140
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:14,000
You're not going to stay with those little ones.
你不会和那些小家伙在一起了。

141
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
Maybe she was being a bit too rough.
也许她太粗暴了些。

142
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:23,000
Nussa lots immediately taking over the babysitting of these little ones, comforting and soothing them.
努萨立刻接手了这些小动物的照顾工作，给予它们安慰和安抚。

143
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:27,000
You can see the effect she's having. They're so much more relaxed.
你可以看到她带来的效果，它们现在放松多了。

144
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,000
And the whole atmosphere has come right down.
整个氛围也变得轻松了许多。

145
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:36,000
So for the first night, these little ones are going to have a very, very big sister.
所以，在第一个晚上，这些小动物将有一位非常大的姐姐。

146
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
And it's not going to be Wendy.
而那位姐姐不会是温迪。

147
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:44,000
But the big question is, what's going to happen to Wendy?
但关键问题是，温迪会怎么样呢？

148
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:48,000
How are they ever going together to bond with the rest of the herd now?
现在，它们要如何与群体中的其他动物建立联系呢？

149
00:14:56,000 --> 00:15:03,000
It's been a few weeks since the little blind calf and dellolo arrived in a terrible state at the Nairobi nursery.
自从那头失明的小牛和德尔洛以糟糕的状态被送到内罗毕育婴室后，已经过了几周了。

150
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
And he's making really good progress.
而它现在正在取得很好的进步。

151
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:13,000
He goes on daily outings and the keepers have come up with a simple and effective way to help him cope.
他每天都会出去活动，而管理员们想出了一种简单有效的办法来帮助他应对这种情况。

152
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:26,000
The first day we took him out, he was very happy to go out with a keeper, trying to make a sound with a stick.
第一天我们带他出去时，他非常高兴能和管理员一起出去，还试图用棍子发出声音。

153
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:30,000
And he actually was following the sound and the keepers were.
实际上，他能够跟随那些声音，而管理员们也能听到这些声音。

154
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:34,000
He knew that because he could not see, could not use his eye.
他知道该听什么声音，因为他看不见，无法用眼睛来感知。

155
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:38,000
And he could use that to direct him to show where the keepers are.
于是他就可以利用这些声音来知道管理员在哪里。

156
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
And he was very happy to spend out the day with a keeper.
他非常高兴能和管理员一起度过这一天。

157
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:49,000
He's got a strong spirit to live. He actually has the desire to go on.
他有着强烈的生存意志，他确实有继续前进的意愿。

158
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:52,000
It's very difficult that he can't see.
他看不见，这确实很困难。

159
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:56,000
You see, he wants to run around the bush and sometimes he's the tree.
你看，他喜欢在灌木丛间奔跑，有时还会躲在树后面。

160
00:15:56,000 --> 00:16:01,000
So he doesn't mind being blind. He wants to behave like a real wild elephant.
所以他并不介意自己失明，他希望自己能像一头真正的野生大象一样生活。

161
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
It's very difficult, he's blind.
非常困难，他失明了。

162
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:11,000
He's still under treatment for his eye condition, but it's too early to tell if it's working.
他仍在接受眼部疾病的治疗，但还无法判断治疗是否有效。

163
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Unfortunately, he's not yet ready to go out with the rest of the orphans.
不幸的是，他还不适合和其他孤儿们一起外出。

164
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:21,000
He could never keep up, let alone cope with the rough and tumble of their daily outings.
他根本无法跟上他们的步伐，更不用说应对他们日常活动的各种挑战了。

165
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,000
In the afternoon, it's often time for a bit of exploration.
下午时，通常是探索的好时机。

166
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:27,000
And today we're taking our little orphans to the quarry.
今天，我们将带着这些小孤儿去采石场。

167
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:34,000
The quarry is full of beautiful, soft, iron-rich red air, and the eddies love it.
采石场里充满了美丽、柔软且富含铁质的红色空气，那些河豚特别喜欢这种环境。

168
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Every time the elephants come to this quarry, they seem to have a good time.
每次大象来到这个采石场时，它们似乎都玩得很开心。

169
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:43,000
They just love to get stuck in and have a good old bus phone.
它们就喜欢被困在里面，好好享受一番。

170
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
It does have a preference.
它们确实有自己的偏好。

171
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,000
It means that it protects him from the sun, gets rid of parasite.
这意味着它能保护他免受阳光伤害，还能驱除寄生虫。

172
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
But you know what? At this stage, I think if you want to see him coming back and just getting dirtier.
但是你知道吗？在现阶段，我觉得如果你希望看到它回来，那它只会变得更脏而已。

173
00:16:54,000 --> 00:17:07,000
This is actually very fun in this bit here.
其实这里的情况挺有趣的。

174
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,000
They seem to be using it as a flight.
他们似乎把这里当作一个飞行平台来使用。

175
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:15,000
And once one elephant does it, another comes along and has a guy.
一旦有一头大象这么做，另一头大象就会过来与它一起玩。

176
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:23,000
But McKenna, the smallest elephant here, is only interested in playing with a herd's mini-matriarch they were laid in.
不过，这里最小的那头大象——麦肯纳，只对与群体中的小型母象一起玩耍感兴趣。

177
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:27,000
These two have a very close and loving bond.
这两头大象之间有着非常亲密且充满爱的关系。

178
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:35,000
And it's one of the wonderful things about elephants, the way they form these deep lifelong friendships with each other.
大象们能形成深厚的终生友谊，这是它们很棒的特点之一。

179
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:44,000
This is something I am hoping to see, as I head back towards the earth on the stockade.
我希望能在返回地球的路上再次看到这种情况。

180
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:51,000
It's been a couple of weeks since I was last here, and I'm hoping that Wendy has started to bond again with the other elephants.
自从上次在这里以来已经过了几周，我希望温迪能再次与其他大象建立联系。

181
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
But first, I want to check out Iraq.
不过首先，我想去看看伊拉克。

182
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:59,000
As the keepers say, he's formed a strong attachment to one of the older elephants.
正如那些饲养员所说，它与其中一头年纪较大的大象建立了深厚的感情。

183
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:02,000
And I've arrived just in time for midday milk.
我刚好在中午时分到达，可以喝到牛奶了。

184
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Look at that, look at the excitement. This is the last group of elephants, and amongst them there, in the middle.
看那，看这兴奋的场景吧。这是最后一群大象，而它们中间就有那头大象。

185
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
That's the one I've been waiting for. That's Iraq.
那就是我一直在等待的那头大象——那就是伊拉克。

186
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:16,000
He's one of the ones that we moved from Nairobi just recently.
它是我们最近从内罗毕运来的大象之一。

187
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:19,000
And he has made a relationship with Nairobi so long.
它与内罗毕建立了长久的关系。

188
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
She's like his mum.
她就像它的妈妈一样。

189
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:25,000
And wherever she goes, he tries to come into the middle here.
无论她去哪里，它都试图跑到中间来。

190
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,000
The tiniest of all.
它是所有大象中最小的一只。

191
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Looking just a touch confused but knows what's good for him.
看起来有点困惑，但他知道什么对自己最有利。

192
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:41,000
And just going and asking, "I think that's nice of life. That's his surrogate mother."
他只是去问：“我觉得那很不错。她就是他的替代母亲。”

193
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Just a touch of nervousness, and you'd expect him.
有点紧张，这是可以理解的。

194
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:50,000
This little elephant didn't come to the orphanage until he was 18 months old.
这只小象在18个月大之前都没有去孤儿院。

195
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:53,000
So he knew all about his wild family.
所以他完全了解自己那混乱的家庭状况。

196
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:58,000
He knew what he was missing. When he was orphaned, his mother got sick, she died.
他知道自己缺少什么。当他成为孤儿时，他的母亲生病了，最终去世了。

197
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:04,000
And a year and a half, he was suddenly torn away from his complete support system.
一年半后，他突然被从完整的支持体系中分离出来。

198
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Look.
看吧。

199
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:11,000
Now, you see, nervous? Where's mum? Where's my new mum?
现在，你看到了吗？很紧张吧？妈妈在哪里？我的新妈妈在哪里？

200
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
He's hit me from the summer.
夏天的时候他打我了。

201
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Where is she? He's on the search, you know.
她在哪里？他在寻找她，你知道的。

202
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Look at the difference between him and the other elephants.
看看他和其他大象的区别。

203
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:24,000
All the other elephants quiet, relaxed, and he's looking for somebody.
其他大象都安静而放松，而他却在寻找某个人。

204
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Here comes Nassau.
纳索来了。

205
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:30,000
See the trunk around.
看他的鼻子吧。

206
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:36,000
And that's what he needs right now.
这正是他现在需要的。

207
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:40,000
He means that we as humans are not enough for him.
他的意思是，作为人类，我们对他来说不够。

208
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:45,000
And that's the reason why Nassau actually joins Iraq.
这就是纳索选择加入伊拉克的原因。

209
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:49,000
To keep him calm, to keep him settled.
为了让他保持冷静，让他安心。

210
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Totally different behavior now.
现在他的行为完全不一样了。

211
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Once more of that big presence behind him, just reassuring.
又有一股强大的力量在他身后，只是带来一种安心感而已。

212
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:58,000
And of course that's what he'd get from his mother.
当然，这也是他从母亲那里得到的回应。

213
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:07,000
One of the things that I love about elephants, and you can see it happening right here in front of you,
我喜欢大象的特质之一，而你可以直接在眼前看到这一点，

214
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,000
is the empathy that they have for one another.
那就是它们彼此之间的同理心。

215
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,000
These two elephants aren't related. It's not a mother and god.
这两头大象并非有亲缘关系，既不是母子关系，也不是亲兄弟关系。

216
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:17,000
But you'd never know it, because they really do seem to care.
但你根本看不出来，因为他们真的很关心这件事。

217
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:21,000
And actually, I think it's essential to Iraq, a little elephant,
实际上，我认为对伊拉克来说，有一头小象的存在非常重要。

218
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,000
to have that kind of nurturing right now.
现在就需要这种关怀与照顾。

219
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:28,000
He needs it, and Nassau lot knows it, and she's prepared to give it to him.
他需要它，纳索的众人也都明白，而她也愿意将其给予他。

220
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
That's just the most wonderful thing.
这真是最美好的事情了。

221
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:34,000
So, life's looking great for Iraq.
所以，伊拉克的局势看起来很不错。

222
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:38,000
And the keepers tell me that the other two little lilies who came up with him
那些人告诉我，与他一起出现的另外两朵小百合花也很好。

223
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
have also settled in really well.
我也已经很好地安顿下来了。

224
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
But what about Wendy?
那温迪呢？

225
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Well, it looks as if things have really turned around for her too.
看来她的情况也真的好转了。

226
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
I mean, just look at Wendy.
我的意思是，只要看看温迪就知道了。

227
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Now when we brought those three little orphans from Nairobi up here to a funder,
当我们把那三个来自内罗毕的孤儿带到这里，寻求资助时，

228
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,000
we thought that Wendy perhaps would adopt the role of the matriarch.
我们觉得温迪或许会扮演母亲的角色。

229
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
She would be like a mother to her, while it didn't happen.
她会像母亲一样照顾他们，但实际上并没有那样发生。

230
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
But look at her now. She's beginning to actually move away from that dependence on people
但现在看看她吧。她开始逐渐摆脱对他人的依赖了。

231
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:09,000
and become an elephant, to be part of the herd.
变成一头大象，成为群中的一员。

232
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
Just to have fun, just to enjoy her.
只是为了娱乐，只是为了享受她。

233
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:17,000
This is if she's growing up a little bit, but very much now, connected with being an elephant.
如果她稍微长大一点，现在她与成为一头大象的关联就更加紧密了。

234
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,000
That's just what we wanted.
这正是我们想要的。

235
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:23,000
So, what could have prompted Wendy's change of heart?
那么，究竟是什么促使温迪改变了想法呢？

236
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Maybe, with throwing new babies in the herd, occupying the keepers' attention.
也许，把新出生的幼崽放进群中，可以分散饲养员的注意力。

237
